sections_expected_source=harness/ENVIRONMENT.md section 9 lines 526-532 and 590, inherited provisioning evidence: '3 Results sections, all Class=config Type=dockerfile: 3 misconfigurations (DS-0026 No HEALTHCHECK defined, LOW). Zero Vulnerabilities, zero Secrets.'
section_vulnerabilities_observed=not established in this record
section_secrets_observed=not established in this record
section_misconfigurations_observed=not established in this record
sections_observed_from_artifact=false
sections_observed_unestablished_reason=the per-section split is a property of harness/artifacts/raw/trivy.json, which is not an input to this record and was absent from this clone when it was written; the runner's stdout carries only the Results-level aggregate. Named as unestablished rather than omitted or inferred (AAP 0.9.4, and 0.1.3 reject rather than infer). No number in this record is fabricated
sections_observed_routes_rejected=re-running the runner would delete this record's own dependency logs and the artifact (run-trivy.sh lines 59-60); an independent re-scan would make one count appear in two documents from two measurements, which AAP 0.6.4 forbids; and a sibling checkout is not this agent's to read
sections_corroboration=every figure the two can be compared on agrees: 3 Results sections observed against 3 inherited, and an artifact of 3496 bytes against 3,496. That is why the inherited breakdown is carried as the expected value and not restated as an observation
sections_sum_identity=Vulnerabilities + Secrets + Misconfigurations equals the trivy record count, which must equal trivy's parsed + rejected in harness/artifacts/logs/normalize-run.json (AAP 0.5.4). Against the expected breakdown that is 0 + 0 + 3 = 3, and against the observed aggregate the record count is 3
sections_sum_identity_owner=harness/artifacts/logs/normalize-run.json owns the parsed and rejected counts; this record owns the section fields the identity is evaluated over
start_line_section_dependence=present on Secrets and Misconfigurations, absent on Vulnerabilities
start_line_absence_permitted=true
start_line_absence_note=AAP 0.8.2 permits absence for severity_native, start_line, cwe, cve and package_coordinate only, so a vulnerability row carrying no line is legitimate rather than a rejection
unattributable_record_policy=a record that cannot be attributed to a section is rejected and counted under its own class, never guessed into one (AAP 0.1.3)
sections_unsupported=Licenses,ExperimentalModifiedFindings
unsupported_section_licenses_empty=true
unsupported_section_experimentalmodifiedfindings_empty=true
unsupported_sections_check_performed=true
unsupported_sections_check_method=run-trivy.sh lines 93-97 add len(res[key]) for both 'Licenses' and 'ExperimentalModifiedFindings' over every Results element of all 18 per-directory reports, and line 118 prints 'UNSUPPORTED NON-EMPTY SECTIONS PRESENT: {...}' if either is non-empty
unsupported_sections_check_evidence=trivy.stdout.log carries no such line while carrying the same block's own output at lines 32-33, which shows the check ran to completion over this run's 18 parts
unsupported_sections_check_scope=all 18 per-directory reports before the merge, which is every Results element the merged artifact contains
unsupported_sections_halt_triggered=false
unsupported_sections_recorded_as=an explicit boolean per unsupported section rather than an omission, because an omitted check looks identical to a passed one and the failure it guards against is real tool output silently dropped while the reconciliation identity still balances
halt_unsupported_finding_section=not triggered
halt_unsupported_finding_section_rule=any non-empty finding array outside the three supported sections halts the run with the observed structure quoted (AAP 0.5.4, 0.9.2)
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections=checked, not triggered
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections_evidence=the merge preserves every section array verbatim and rewrites only Results[].Target (run-trivy.sh lines 100-109), so section membership - the sole basis for scanner_class - survives into the merged artifact
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections_artifact_level_owner=harness/lib/normalize/adapters/trivy.py, whose halt classes unsupported_finding_section, unknown_finding_section and supported_section_not_an_array are evaluated when the artifact itself is read
scanners_enabled=vuln,secret,misconfig
baked_flags=--scanners vuln,secret,misconfig --format json --output <per-directory part> --skip-db-update --skip-java-db-update --skip-check-update --offline-scan --no-progress --quiet
baked_flags_source=run-trivy.sh lines 67-71, summarised at trivy.stdout.log line 12
invocation_form=one `trivy fs <one root-relative path>` per scope directory, 18 invocations
